		"name": "MuleSoft Hello World API",
		"description": "Postman collection for testing the MuleSoft Hello World application.\n\n## About\n- **Application**: mulesoft-hello-world\n- **Base URL**: http://localhost:8081\n- **Version**: 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT\n- **Runtime**: Mule 4.x\n\n## Endpoints\n- GET /hello - Returns a Hello World message\n\n## Usage\n1. Ensure the MuleSoft application is running in Anypoint Studio\n2. Import this collection into Postman\n3. Run individual requests or the entire collection\n\n## Test Results\n- Load tested with 36,100 requests\n- 100% success rate\n- Peak throughput: 7,102 req/sec",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "12345678"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Health Check",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get Hello World",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// Test 1: Status code should be 200",
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Test 2: Response time should be less than 200ms",
									"pm.test(\"Response time is less than 200ms\", function () {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Test 3: Content-Type should be text/plain",
									"pm.test(\"Content-Type is text/plain\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.header(\"Content-Type\");",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"text/plain\");",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Test 4: Response body should contain expected text",
									"pm.test(\"Response body contains 'Hello World from MuleSoft!'\", function () {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.equal(\"Hello World from MuleSoft!\");",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Test 5: Response should not be empty",
									"pm.test(\"Response body is not empty\", function () {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.be.empty;",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Log response details",
									"console.log(\"Response Time: \" + pm.response.responseTime + \"ms\");",
									"console.log(\"Response Body: \" + pm.response.text());"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						},
